Status: [x] done  |  [] open  |  [Deprecated] implemented then removed, retired, or disabled from the product surface

================================================================================
SEARCH RESULTS DISPLAY
================================================================================

[x] Show results on a map with each point labeled with the rental price

[x] Present search results optionally as a cards grid in addition to the table view (grid vs list toggle). Cards are clickable and open the listing in a new tab; map is preserved.

[x] Map labels: optional price vs rank toggle. Rank uses a circle with a large bold number; price uses a rectangle with smaller non-bold font.

[x] Store the currently displayed result set as a variable (display_list / master_list), rather than looking it up from the latest chat message. The dataframe and map always point at that result set.

[x] When filtering, keep a master list of all listings from the search API and a filtered list when filters are applied. Relaxing filters reuses the master list without calling the search API again unless necessary.

[x] Show a score column in the results table when available. The column is now "Match score" (overall match_score, falling back to semantic_score).

[x] Give the agent the ability to search multiple locations at once and combine the results into a single list. This would require calling the search tool multiple times (in parallel) and merging the results.

================================================================================
SEARCH MARKETS / BACKENDS
================================================================================

[Deprecated] Open the search tool to US and India cities in addition to Canada (all countries supported by pyRealtor).
    pyRealtor was retired (bot protection / reliability). The current backend is Apify Realtor.ca (Canada only). SEARCH_MARKET=us is reserved in backends/base.py but not implemented; India is not planned.

================================================================================
PREFERENCES
================================================================================

[x] Store user search preferences and reuse them so the agent does not re-ask (budget, beds, baths, den, size, proximity, qualitative). Persisted to ~/.rental_search_agent/preferences.json.

[x] Extend preferences to capture geographic proximity as open text (e.g. max 30 min drive to downtown, max 5 min walk to a SkyTrain station, 20 min drive to a work address). The LLM parses this into structured rules.

[x] Extend preferences to capture unstructured listing preferences (e.g. balcony, parking, gym).

[Deprecated] Store viewing-time / name / email in the preferences UI so the agent does not re-ask for bookings.
    Contact keys (viewing_preference, name, email, phone) are still persisted in preferences.json but are hidden from the sidebar and are not injected into the agent system prompt. Chat booking is disabled.

================================================================================
PROXIMITY
================================================================================

[x] Geocode locations referenced in proximity preferences (once at the start of a search, and again after proximity prefs change).

[x] Geocoding needs a real address. The LLM is instructed to disambiguate terms such as "Downtown Vancouver" to an actual address.

[x] Measure proximity (km, minutes walk / drive / transit) of listings to preferred locations and append those measures to search results (enrich_listings_with_proximity).

[x] Filter results using those proximity measures via filter_listings (proximity_rules).

[x] Nearest transit / train station geolocations.
    Implemented via Google Places Nearby Search at enrichment time (not a static placeholder). "nearest transit station" is skipped during geocoding and resolved per listing.

================================================================================
SCORING AND ANALYSIS
================================================================================

[x] Apply user preferences to search results (structural filters, proximity, qualitative).

[x] Semantic scoring from the user query/preferences vs listing description (cosine similarity).

[x] Complement cosine similarity with other scoring methods.
    Multi-metric match_score: structural, proximity, amenity, and semantic components (match_scoring.py). Ranking by preferences is optional because it is expensive.

[x] LLM-based listing analysis against preferences (Analyze link → dedicated analysis card).
    Shows match score (%), key matches, and key gaps.

================================================================================
VIEWING AND CALENDAR
================================================================================

[Deprecated] Force the agent to show a dropdown for selecting listings to submit a viewing request for.
    ask_user dropdown/multiselect still exists for search clarification. The viewing shortlist flow (build_approval_choices) is unused: chat is search/refine only.

[Deprecated] Google Calendar tools (list / create / update / delete events) and book viewings from preferred timeslots before submitting a viewing request.
    Tools still exist in server.py / client.py TOOLS, but they are excluded from the chat agent (CHAT_DISABLED_TOOL_NAMES). MCP server still exposes them.

[Deprecated] Let the user adjust a draft viewing schedule (add/remove listings, change viewing time).
    modify_viewing_plan still exists but is chat-disabled (same as calendar tools).

[] Implement a true viewing_request tool. Today booking uses simulate_viewing_request (simulated; also chat-disabled). Real flow: listing URL → "Request a showing" → fill personal details and time → check "I'm not a robot" → submit.

[] Each result card should have a "Request a viewing" button, disabled if the listing is already on the viewing schedule. Clicking it should: check calendar for slots in preferred viewing times, present slots for approval, book the selected slot, then submit a viewing request.

================================================================================
UX
================================================================================

[x] Streaming agent responses in the chat interface.

[x] Status indicators while tools run (e.g. "Searching for listings...", "Filtering listings...", "Ranking listings by your preferences...").

[x] Chat in a floating panel on the bottom-right that scrolls independently of the results panel.

================================================================================
BUGS (PROXIMITY / RANKING)
================================================================================

[x] Proximity limits were computed but not applied as a filter.
    Fixed: filter_listings with proximity_rules after enrich_listings_with_proximity.

[x] Ranking by proximity did not work ("rank the listings by their proximity to my work location").
    Fixed in code: filter_listings sort_by="proximity"; agent instructions require nearest-first sort after enrich; UI no longer clobbers that sort with match_score when last_sort_by is proximity.

[x] When proximity preferences are not provided, the agent still called parse_proximity_preferences, geocode_proximity_references, and enrich_listings_with_proximity.
    Fixed: step 4p has an explicit entry condition.

[x] When applying proximity preferences, enrich_listings_with_proximity was occasionally skipped, so proximity data was missing.
    Fixed: step 4p requires enrich before filter_listings with proximity_rules.

[x] Filter on cheap structural features (beds, baths, size, rent) before expensive enrich_listings_with_proximity / score_listings_by_preferences.
    Fixed: step 3b structural narrow (predicate push-down).

[x] Apify scraper silently fails to scrape some listings. Investigate the issue and add a retry mechanism with exponential backoff.
    Transient run failure/timeout: retry with exponential backoff (APIFY_MAX_RETRIES / APIFY_RETRY_BASE_SECONDS).
    Partial fetchDetails (SUCCEEDED but missing descriptions): WARNING only, no re-scrape.

